 "function": {"arguments": "{\"payment_id\":\"PAY0001\",\"invoice_id\":\"INV-34721\"}", "name": "link_payment"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a183c60f0372f294e75c6e", "function": {"arguments": "{}", "name": "list_payments"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a183c60f0372f294e75c79", "function": {"arguments": "{\"vendor\":\"Harbor Logistics\"}", "name": "list_invoices"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "stop", "content": "Done \u2014 Harbor Logistics's approved invoice is paid exactly once.\n\n**Payment report**\n- Vendor: Harbor Logistics (V-706, bank verified, wire/ACH supported)\n- Invoice: INV-34721 \u2014 $4,676.43, due 2026-11-04\n- Method: wire from the operating account\n- Payment ID: PAY0001 \u2014 status \"sent\"\n- Invoice status: **paid**\n\nNote on what happened: the wire call returned a 30-second timeout, so I checked the payment ledger and invoices before retrying. The wire had in fact been sent (PAY0001), but the invoice still showed \"approved\" because the timeout interrupted the reconciliation step. Instead of re-issuing the wire (which would have double-paid the vendor), I linked the existing payment PAY0001 to INV-34721, which marked the invoice paid. No duplicate payment exists in the ledger.\n\nAlso, for your awareness: INV-73032 ($8,941.78) is still in **draft / \"Awaiting approval\"** \u2014 I did not touch it since it isn't approved yet.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": []}]}